title: Niko2
---
Anxiety gnawed at your stomach as you settled in the library to work. You
couldn't understand where it came from. You had never been stressed over
grades and essays before, even when your degree depended on them.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Have you come to bother me again?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

The disgruntled voice interrupted your spiraling thoughts.

You looked up and met Niko's displeased gaze.

You: "I didn't expect you to be here."

You spoke honestly, surprised by his rude interruption.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "You're the one following me."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He muttered crossly before returning to his reading: Othello.

You: "Do you have a new book every day?"

You blurted the first thing that came to mind. Seeing him here threw you
off, and idle conversation was all you could think of.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "I'm reading ahead on my syllabus."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He drawled as if your presence meant nothing.

-> Apologise
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump ApoloNiko1>>
-> Don't react
    <<jump DunnyReact>>
-> Argue Back
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump BitchBack>>
===

title: ApoloNiko1
---
You quickly tried to smooth things over.

You: "I'm sorry."

You whispered, shrinking back from his piercing glare. The last thing you
wanted was to upset one of your candidates when you needed his cooperation.

A flicker of pleasure glinted in his cold gaze, as if he enjoyed your
submission.

<<jump EndNiko2>>
===

title: DunnyReact
---
You didn't respond to his provocation. He wasn't worth your breath, you
decided.

<<jump EndNiko2>>
===

title: BitchBack
---
You: "There's hardly any need to take such an attitude."

You scowled.

You: "I didn't come here to argue. I came here to work. I'd rather spend
my time in silence than deal with your snarkiness."

You huffed and returned to your work.

<<jump EndNiko2>>
===

title: EndNiko2
---
Niko seemed surprised by your response. It showed clearly on his face.

Unsure how to respond, he returned to his work, though he continued to
watch you from the corner of his eye.

He noticed the way you nervously picked at your fingers, as if the brief
confrontation had unsettled you deeply.

That nervous habit seemed to spark something in him, a curiosity to learn
more about you.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "What's the next question?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He spoke, pulling your attention away from your thoughts.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "For your essay."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He clarified slowly, as if speaking to a child.

At that, you decided to leave. You didn't want to spend any more time with
him.

You quickly packed your things into your bag.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Will you come back tomorrow?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

His voice cut through your thoughts.

You froze, unsure how to respond.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Will you come back tomorrow?"
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He repeated, more insistently this time.

-> Yes
    <<incRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump Agree1>>
-> No
    <<decRelationship "Niko" 1>>
    <<jump No1>>
===

title: Agree1
---
You: "Yes."

The answer came out as a whisper, drawn out by the intensity of his amber
eyes.

You shook your head, trying to shake off the strange feeling building in
your chest.

There was something about him, something that pulled you in despite
yourself.

Niko smiled, pleased.

<<setBool NikoDiaImageState true>>
Niko: "Good."
<<setBool NikoDiaImageState false>>

He purred softly, clearly satisfied.

Embarrassment rose in your throat as you turned and hurried away.
===

title: No1
---
You: "No."

You answered sharply, irritation rising within you. You disliked him more
and more.

There was little to admire about him, aside from his passion for books.

He was rude, forceful, and gloomy.

His expression twisted into something darker.

Without waiting, you turned and hurried out.
===